d have blessed that too. Both stay drifted on the owner's brief.\n\nThe correction is drafted in this spec's `## Dispositions` (commit `d9f717d6`), validated through `intake.parse_dispositions` (no refusal, `kind=spine`): fix the cell, then take the withheld anchor over the LLR registry alone — one act that also re-anchors `LLR-136` and the WI-566 set. No registry cell and no `Status` cell was touched.\n\nOne caveat on the bar: `format` skipped on both commits (ruff not importable by this box's `python3`). Nothing Python changed, but the step did not run and I am not claiming it green."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1507,"cache_read_input_tokens":111364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1507},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a7dbb3f-72e7-4456-8f3b-e892ea528da0","uuid":"8b78d854-4ae9-43b9-b748-1fe74e46ff7d","request_id":"req_011CeeU495So7vk1czV6y5y9"}
